@meeting train.m13.calder
// Pillar 5 Step 4, M13 leak hunting: Calder at your first drip, when she's the one on shift who teaches it. Seat E2.
// Head writer W2.
title: Follow the wet
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder showed you leak hunting: read the puddle, follow the wet back to the joint, then tighten or replace it.
== lines
calder: A drip. Look before you touch anything.   [gesture]
calder > you: Which way is it running? Read the puddle. Wetter is closer.
calder: Find the joint. Tighten it a quarter turn at a time. Worn through, replace it.
calder: Drips don't fix themselves. They get bigger. Go.
